  <p class="section-label">05 / Beyond the answer</p>
  <h2 id="trajectory">A cognitive trajectory, not a terminal output.</h2>

  <p>MetaMind addresses the first part of a broader research program. Cognitive AI expands the basic unit of intelligence from an answer to a trajectory: understand another mind before action, monitor and revise cognition during action, then model how that action changes the world over time.</p>

  <section class="cognitive-trajectory trajectory-map" aria-label="Cognitive AI research trajectory">
    <canvas data-cognitive-trajectory aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
    <header class="trajectory-heading"><span>Cognitive AI</span><strong>One answer. A longer trajectory.</strong><p>Before → during → after action</p></header>
    <ol>
      <li><span>Before action</span><strong>Infer minds.</strong><p>Reason over beliefs, desires, boundaries, roles, uncertainty, and what remains unobserved.</p></li>
      <li><span>During action</span><strong>Monitor cognition.</strong><p>Expose where a reasoning path diverges, compare alternatives, and revise before the error becomes an intervention.</p></li>
      <li><span>After action</span><strong>Model consequences.</strong><p>Track how advice, comfort, negotiation, or refusal changes decisions, relationships, and future possibilities.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="trajectory-outcomes" aria-label="Three ways an action changes the world"><b>Action changes</b><div><span>Decision</span><span>Relationship</span><span>Future state</span></div></div>
  </section>

  <p>A language-only system can describe a world while failing to model how its own action changes that world. The next step is therefore not a better vocabulary for reasoning. It is a cognitive world model: physical state determines what can happen; mental and social state help determine which possibility an agent chooses, how others respond, and which future becomes reachable.</p>

  <div class="limit-note"><p><strong>Boundary of the present work.</strong> MetaMind is evaluated mainly in constrained textual settings. Multimodal cues, cultural variation, group dynamics, durable relationships, privacy, and long-horizon causal effects remain open. The framework is evidence for explicit, revisable social inference—not a claim that those broader problems are solved.</p></div>

  <p>The answer is a point in time. Cognition begins before it, remains active while it forms, and continues through the world it helps create.</p>

